  overview: [
    "The actions row sits under a hairline rule, a ghost cancel before the primary submit; each FormSection closes with the same rule. A `disabled` form dims as a whole and disables its actions.",
    "`twoColumn` lays the rows out in exactly two equal columns 16px apart, however wide the form: the fields fill their columns left to right, an odd last field keeps its half, and a FormSection takes the whole row, after which the next field starts a new one. The form measures itself, and at 512px or narrower (the `lg` width step) the rows stack in one full-width column instead.",
    "`FormSection aside` sets the section's heading in a rail beside its rows, the layout of a settings page: the rail at the `xs` width step (320px), 48px from the rows, a 20px title over a 14px description, the rows 18px apart, 28px above and below the rows and a rule closing the section. The section measures itself, and at 512px or narrower (the `lg` width step) the rail stacks over the rows. A form whose last row is an aside section drops the actions row's rule (the section's closes the rows). `hints` puts leading content in the actions row, before the buttons (the keyboard hints \"↵ to save\"), and the row then spreads the two to its ends.",
  ],
